2026-10-31T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-2377) 'Why each platform bakes
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2377  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-2377) 'The program hash covers the machine layout as well as the program, so C baked on one
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2377  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-2377) 'platform does not match on another. Windows and Linux on x86_64 share a layout and a hash,
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2377  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:27Z (RFD66606-2377) 'and each still compiles its own copy. One bake of the SolidCraft guest is 32 C files, 336
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2377  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:28Z (RFD66606-2377) 'MB of C for 16.2 MB of RISC-V code.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2377  1 LINE
 Text:Written

